Absolutely.  The first thing you need to do is identify - on the SAN - the
connection - i.e. the FC adapter in
the Tru64 box.  I'd rename the connection based on the host name of the
machine... To identify the connection
look at the wwid of the FC adapter on Tru64 machine.  You can get this from
hwmgr (it's one of the flags
-XXXXserial_number or something to that affect.  Then match it up on the
SAN(by doing a show conn)

Note: the prefix of the wwid may be different on the controller than it is
on the UNIX box.  For example,
I believe it goes:

UNIX box:

1000-xxxx-xxxx...

On the SAN:

2000-xxxx-xxxx...

Where the xxxx's match exactly.  Then on the SAN do

set UNIT enable=CONNECTION

for example:

set d34 enable=host_1,host_2

James.

